<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rawal Jaisal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rawal Jaisal was a Bhati <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> ruler who founded the city and fort of Jaisalmer in 1156. Leaving the older capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodurva">Lodurva</a>, he built his stronghold on the Trikuta hill in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thar-desert">Thar Desert</a>. The yellow sandstone fort became the heart of a kingdom that grew rich on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rawal-jaisal.jpg" alt="Rawal Jaisal" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Archan dave · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rawal_Jaisal_Singh,_the_founder_and_first_ruler_of_the_Kingdom_of_Jaisalmer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
